From: "claude[bot]" <41898282+claude[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 06:14:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Skip deck-mounted instruments in motion planning and
 offset calibration

Three head-geometry paths that are newer than the CubOS the CubXL runs
(496819c), so the first form of the stirrer change never met them:

- routing._build_scene_from_context builds a tool envelope for every
  instrument and, on a planning-enabled deck, refuses to run if one lacks a
  motion_envelope. A deck-mounted instrument has neither, so only head
  instruments are now required and built.
- gantry.offset_calibration.calibrate_instrument_offsets needs a capture of
  every instrument except lighting. A stirrer can't be brought to the mark,
  so deck-mounted entries are now left out, and one can't be the reference.
- build_instrumented_gantry refuses a motion_envelope on a deck-mounted
  instrument, as the loader already refuses its offsets and depth.

Refs vertical-cloud-lab/byu-vcl#133

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
